# The alternate screen: modes 47, 1047, 1048 and 1049.

test mode 1049 switches to a blank alternate screen
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 1 0 4 9 h: switch to the Alternate Screen Buffer, clearing it first
size 10 4
feed main\e[?1049h
alt-screen on
screen
| |

test mode 1049 brings the normal screen back
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 1 0 4 9 l: use Normal Screen Buffer and restore the cursor
size 10 4
feed main\e[?1049hALT\e[?1049l
alt-screen off
screen
|main|

test mode 1049 saves the cursor and restores it
spec xterm ctlseqs 1049: save the cursor as in DECSC on entry, restore as in DECRC on exit
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3Hmain\e[?1049h\e[4;4Hx\e[?1049l
cursor 2,7

test mode 1049 leaves the cursor where it is
spec xterm ctlseqs 1049 combines 1047 and 1048, neither of which moves the cursor
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3H\e[?1049hx
screen
| |
|  x|
cursor 2,4

test mode 1049 clears the alternate screen each time
spec xterm ctlseqs 1049: clearing it first
size 10 4
feed \e[?1049hX\e[?1049l\e[?1049h
screen
| |

test mode 1049 restores the rendition saved with the cursor
spec xterm ctlseqs 1049: save and restore the cursor as in DECSC and DECRC (which keep the SGR attributes)
size 10 4
feed \e[31m\e[?1049h\e[0m\e[?1049lx
cell 1,1 text=x fg=idx:1

test the normal screen is not touched while the alternate one shows
spec xterm ctlseqs: two screen buffers
size 10 4
feed main\e[?1049h\e[2J\e[HALT\e[?1049l
screen
|main|

test the alternate screen has no saved lines
spec xterm ctlseqs, The Alternate Screen Buffer: contains no additional saved lines
size 10 3
feed \e[?1049h1\r\n2\r\n3\r\n4\r\n5
screen
|3|
|4|
|5|
scrollback-len 0

test the normal screen's saved lines survive a visit to the alternate screen
spec xterm ctlseqs, The Alternate Screen Buffer: the Normal Screen Buffer keeps its saved lines
size 10 3
feed 1\r\n2\r\n3\r\n4\e[?1049h5\r\n6\r\n7\r\n8\e[?1049l
scrollback
|1|

test mode 1047 clears the alternate screen when leaving it
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 1 0 4 7 l: clear the screen first if in the Alternate Screen Buffer
known-fail: alacritty – CSI ? 1047 h/l is ignored: the alternate screen never shows
size 10 4
feed \e[?1047hX\e[?1047l\e[?1047h
alt-screen on
screen
| |

test mode 1047 does not save the cursor
spec xterm ctlseqs: 1047 only switches the buffer; 1048 is the one that saves the cursor
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3H\e[?1047h\e[4;4H\e[?1047l
cursor 4,4

test mode 1047 brings back the normal screen
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 1 0 4 7 l: Use Normal Screen Buffer
known-fail: alacritty – CSI ? 1047 h/l is ignored: the alternate screen never shows
size 10 4
feed main\e[?1047hALT\e[?1047l
alt-screen off
screen
|main|

test mode 1048 saves and restores the cursor
spec xterm ctlseqs 1048: save the cursor as in DECSC, restore it as in DECRC
known-fail: alacritty – CSI ? 1048 h/l is ignored: the cursor is not restored
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3H\e[?1048h\e[4;4H\e[?1048l
cursor 2,3
alt-screen off

test mode 47 uses the alternate screen
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 4 7 h: Use Alternate Screen Buffer (only the buffer changes: the cursor stays, as for 1047 and 1049); CSI ? 4 7 l: Use Normal Screen Buffer
known-fail: alacritty – CSI ? 47 h/l is ignored: the alternate screen never shows
size 10 4
feed main\e[?47hALT
alt-screen on
screen
|    ALT|
feed \e[?47l
alt-screen off
screen
|main|

test mode 47 keeps what the alternate screen showed
convention the xterm text only says 1049 and 1047 clear; 47 just switches buffers
size 10 4
feed \e[?47hX\e[?47l\e[?47h
screen
|X|

test leaving the alternate screen twice is harmless
convention a reset of a mode that is already reset changes nothing
size 10 4
feed main\e[?1049h\e[?1049l\e[?47lx
alt-screen off
screen
|mainx|

test mode 1049 again on the alternate screen changes nothing
spec xterm ctlseqs 1049: use the Alternate Screen Buffer, clearing it first; the clearing belongs to the switch, which asking again does not make
size 10 4
feed \e[?1049hX\e[?1049h
alt-screen on
screen
|X|
